From 66a2b43d55408ba57943cab7ce99b1990ecdcf38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:26:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(cron): a fire whose gateway socket never opened
 is held, not booked FAILED

run_canonical_job booked a fire FAILED when connect_gateway could not open the
WebSocket (GatewayClientError 'Gateway connection failed; no local fallback',
raised from an OSError/TimeoutError) although nothing was submitted and no
admission journal existed. hermes-hub 2026-11-13 05:20 UTC: a core-update drain
released 31 deferred cron jobs, the gateway loop stalled ~4 s, and three jobs
(6b4342ad83d9 and two others) were booked FAILED.

A dial failure before submit now raises CronFireNotAdmitted('unreachable',
'connect_failed'), so a scheduled fire is held and its slot stays due. The hold
count lives in last_fire_error.connect_holds; after CONNECT_HOLD_LIMIT (3)
consecutive dial-failure holds the next one is booked FAILED as before, so a
gateway that stays unreachable still alerts. Owner refusals, not-ready verdicts,
local client refusals and any failure after submit are unchanged.

release_unadmitted_fire moves from cron/jobs.py to cron/unadmitted_fire.py
(offsets the file-size ratchet; sole caller updated).
